subquestions.resolution_criteria:
This question resolves Yes if, between 2025-11-10 and 2025-12-10 (inclusive), Valve Corporation officially announces or reveals a new game that continues the Half-Life series.

For this subquestion, an "officially announces or reveals" event means at least one of the following occurs during the resolution window:
1. Valve publishes an announcement on its official news channels explicitly identifying a new Half-Life game (for example, on the Valve Steam news hub at https://store.steampowered.com/news/publisher/valve or another official Valve-owned site);
2. Valve publishes an official trailer, teaser, or reveal video for such a game on an official Valve channel such as https://www.youtube.com/@Valve ;
3. Valve creates a publicly accessible official Steam store page for a new Half-Life title published by Valve at https://store.steampowered.com/ ;
4. Valve makes an official public statement naming or clearly presenting a new game as a continuation of the Half-Life series.

"Continuing the Half-Life series" includes a title called Half-Life 3 or a differently titled game that is clearly presented by Valve as a new installment/sequel/follow-up in the Half-Life franchise. Remasters, ports, soundtrack releases, documentaries, patches, merchandise, or unrelated Valve titles do not count. A non-Valve rumor, leak, press report, datamine, or third-party event mention does not count unless Valve itself publicly confirms it during the window.

Primary resolution sources: Valve Steam news hub (https://store.steampowered.com/news/publisher/valve), the Steam store itself (https://store.steampowered.com/search/?publisher=Valve), Valve's official YouTube channel (https://www.youtube.com/@Valve), and Valve's official website (https://www.valvesoftware.com/).

If no qualifying official announcement/reveal occurs between 2025-11-10 and 2025-12-10 (inclusive), this question resolves No. If an event is only rumored during the window and officially confirmed only after 2025-12-10, it does not count. If Valve's official channels are unavailable, contemporaneous archived copies (for example via the Internet Archive at https://web.archive.org/) or reliable secondary reporting quoting the official Valve post may be used as fallback evidence of what Valve published within the window.
